WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.960
Hello, I'm Jamal Johnson.

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:06.410
You may know me from athletic podcasting

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:10.900
but you might not know I'm
also a renowned art critic.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:12.750
And I am here on Los Feliz,

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:15.550
one of Los Angeles whitest neighborhoods

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:18.000
to critique Black Lives Matter art.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.830
I didn't go to any official
schools or art programs

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:23.510
but I did attend the school of hard knock.

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:26.141
Let's go see how long it
takes for me to get arrested.

00:00:26.141 --> 00:00:29.150
(calm music)

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:31.950
Whenever I see high quality
printouts like this,

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:33.400
I say to myself,

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.180
thank goodness a white person
has felt strongly enough

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.440
about my people being shot by the police

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:41.460
to email a high res
photo to FedEx Kinko's.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:44.220
This next one has a
bit of an outsider art,

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:47.520
Daniel Johnston Esq. kind of field,

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.510
by which I mean it's bad, it's pretty bad.

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:53.060
It's very, very thin, very
uniform lines, very Tim Burton.

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:55.110
Of course this building
doesn't have any signs at all

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:57.820
but these little babies
are kinda hard though.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:59.850
The handcrafted nature of this sign

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:02.370
lets me know that these white people

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:04.350
are actually broke as fuck.

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:07.200
And maybe they didn't do
that well in high school.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.610
This is a truly thin to fine print.

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:11.500
You have to look very close.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:12.850
You have to pull out a Monaco

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:16.890
to see if these people really
think black lives matter.

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:18.440
Also they definitely took this sign

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:19.740
from their restaurant job.

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:22.850
This may just actually be a brunch menu.

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:24.650
Yeah, like this is just some gang shit

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:28.450
but it's good to know the
neighborhood still has a pulse.

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:29.420
Oh my God, guys come here.

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:30.640
Follow me.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:31.769
Look at this.

00:01:31.769 --> 00:01:32.852
Look at this.

00:01:33.727 --> 00:01:35.780
This is what I'm talking about.

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:37.660
This is what we're looking for.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:38.493
Real art.

00:01:38.493 --> 00:01:40.650
Apparently these white homeowners,

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:43.600
who benefited from systemic racism,

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:45.750
want to dismantle it now.

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:47.320
I can't believe what I'm seeing.

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:49.930
They also added the popular slogan, ACAB,

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:52.280
which stands for All Cops Are Bastards,

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:53.610
which is impressive

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:56.422
because their uncle is
the chief of police.

00:01:56.422 --> 00:01:58.803
And so what have we learned today?

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:01.293
Not much, to be honest.

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:03.330
Do black lives matter?

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:04.163
Absolutely.

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:07.080
Aside from that, art is what you make it.

00:02:08.096 --> 00:02:13.096
When you decide to show
your support for black lives

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:16.683
just know that I don't care
about you in the slightest.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:18.353
Art!

